@title Rotating load balancer TLS certificates by hand
@subtitle Edge team · Sycamore Travel

# Certificates

table = Domain,Expires,Days left; www.sycamoretravel.example,2026-11-14,29; api.sycamoretravel.example,2026-11-02,17; partners.sycamoretravel.example,2027-01-20,96; status.sycamoretravel.example,2026-10-30,14

!! status.sycamoretravel.example is the most urgent certificate. It expires 2026-10-30, in 14 days.

# Steps

1. Request the new certificate in the certificate manager.
2. Validate it through the DNS record.
3. Wait for the status Issued.

!! Never remove the old certificate first. Clients will get handshake errors until the new one is attached.

4. Attach the new certificate to the listener on edge-alb-prod.
5. Test with an external checker.
6. Remove the old certificate after 24 hours.

! The automated renewal job is broken until ticket EDGE-812 is fixed. That is why this is manual for now.
